  "verdict": "void",
  "section": "116",
  "quote": "A landlord shall not increase the rent charged to a tenant for a rental unit without first giving the tenant at least 90 days written notice of the landlord’s intention to do so.",
  "reason": "Section 116(1) requires a landlord to give at least 90 days' written notice before increasing the rent. Because the clause purports to allow a rent increase with only 30 days' written notice, it is inconsistent with the Act and therefore void under section 4(1)."
}

